## 20. Sigma Rules

Sigma is a generic and structured detection rule format that can be translated into different SIEM query languages.

A Sigma rule may define:

- Rule title
- Description
- Log source
- Detection logic
- Severity
- Tags
- References
- False-positive guidance
- Author
- Status

Sigma rules support portability across security monitoring platforms.

---

## 21. YARA Rules

YARA is used to identify and classify malware or suspicious files based on patterns.

YARA may support:

- Malware detection
- File classification
- Threat research
- Incident response
- Malware hunting
- Digital forensics

YARA rules should be tested carefully to avoid:

- Excessive false positives
- Overly broad matches
- Performance issues
- Unintended file classification

