## 23. Threat Intelligence and Vulnerability Management

Threat intelligence can improve vulnerability prioritization.

A vulnerability may require increased attention when:

- It is actively exploited.
- It affects critical assets.
- It is associated with known campaigns.
- Exploit code is publicly available.
- It affects internet-facing systems.
- It impacts operational technology.
- It affects unsupported systems.
- It can enable privilege escalation.
- It can support ransomware activity.

Risk-based prioritization should consider:

- Asset criticality
- Exploitability
- Exposure
- Business impact
- Threat activity
- Compensating controls
- Availability requirements
- Safety requirements in OT environments

